    <statement><p>Find a vector equation for the line through the point P = (1, 4, -5) and
parallel to the vector <m>\mathbf{v}</m> = (-5, 3, -4).</p>
<p>Assume <m>\mathbf{r}(0) = 1\!\mathbf{i} + 4\!\mathbf{j}  - 5\!\mathbf{k}</m> 
and that <m>\mathbf{v}</m> is the velocity vector of the line..</p>
<p><m>\mathbf{r}(t)</m> = 
<fillin characters="10" name="AnSwEr0001"/> <m>\mathbf{i}</m> +
<fillin characters="10" name="AnSwEr0002"/> <m>\mathbf{j}</m> +
<fillin characters="10" name="AnSwEr0003"/> <m>\mathbf{k}</m></p>
<p>Rewrite this in terms of the parametric equations for the line.</p>
<p>x = <fillin characters="10" name="AnSwEr0004"/></p>
<p>y = <fillin characters="10" name="AnSwEr0005"/></p>
<p>z = <fillin characters="10" name="AnSwEr0006"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>1+\left(-5\right)t</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
